+# V171 Manual Bank Audit Evidence Index
+
+Release: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.171-manual-bank-audit-index`
+
+## Change
+
+Migration `0124-manual-bank-audit-evidence-index` adds the non-unique partial
+index `audit_manual_bank_payout_paid_evidence` to the audit table:
+
+```sql
+CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS audit_manual_bank_payout_paid_evidence
+  ON audit(target,user_id,created_at)
+  WHERE event='manual_bank_payout_paid';
+```
+
+Manual-bank payout verification always filters on the literal
+`manual_bank_payout_paid` event before it matches the transaction target,
+recording user and timestamp. The partial index therefore covers the evidence
+count and exact-timestamp lookups while excluding unrelated audit events. This
+avoids full audit-table scans as the operational history grows and limits the
+write cost to the relevant paid-evidence rows.
+
+## Integrity behavior
+
+The index is deliberately non-unique. The payout evidence logic treats a
+duplicate paid audit as conflicting evidence and fails closed for review.
+Enforcing uniqueness at the database layer would change that behavior into a
+constraint error, could prevent migration on a database that already contains
+duplicate evidence, and would remove the application's ability to report the
+corruption explicitly. The index improves lookup performance without weakening
+or replacing the existing exact-cardinality checks.
+
+## Verification
+
+- SQLite query-plan checks confirm that both paid-evidence queries use the
+  covering partial index instead of scanning the audit table;
+- isolated PostgreSQL 18 catalog checks confirm the index is non-unique,
+  partial, and ordered as `target,user_id,created_at`;
+- the Render startup migration creates the index and records migration `0124`
+  exactly once, with a second startup remaining idempotent;
+- readiness validation requires the new migration marker after migration
+  `0123-guard-function-schema-binding`;
+- targeted migration, readiness and query-plan checks passed 23/23;
+- SQLite manual-bank checks passed 19/19 and isolated PostgreSQL 18
+  manual-bank checks passed 6/6;
+- backup/report checks passed 19/19, Render database checks passed 3/3,
+  maintenance checks passed 12/12 and release probes passed 27/27;
+- TypeScript, lint and diff checks passed.
+
+## Scope
+
+- no application business state, payment status, wallet balance, reservation
+  or ledger row is changed;
+- no deposit, payout, game-launch, real-payment, live-game or production-ready
+  flag is changed;
+- no table or column is added, removed or rebuilt, and the database table count
+  remains 76;
+- backup schema remains `0122-acceptance-ledger-integrity`; the encrypted
+  backup format and backup table inventory are unchanged;
+- critical database guard attestation remains 9/9 triggers and 5/5 functions;
+- validation made no live payment-provider, game-provider, customer-money or
+  wallet call;
+- this release is a staging candidate and is not production live.
